  Only on the Plane of Fire, imho.

  On the Planes of Earth and Air cursed gold detection saves 
having to get confused/unconfused.  You do have to remember
where the portal is, but even a general location is useful
on those planes.  Again, imho.

  On the Plane of Water cursed gold detection scrolls provide a 
quick, easy way to zero in on the *moving* portal.  It doesn't 
get much better than that.  


  I speak from experience, having tried several times to use the 
confuse/read/unconfuse technique to find the portal when in the 
middle of the Plane of Water.  Also, it may take more than one 
turn to get unconfused.  

  And if you use an expired spell to (try to) get, you may have 
to deal with stunning as well, as well as risking not getting 
confused in the first place.

  If you're not using an expired spell to get confused, you're
burning up other resources instead, which is very problematic
on the plane of Water.  And you still have to get unconfused.


  Furthermore, confused gold detection on the Plane of Water 
prevents you from finding the portal through searching.  The
explicit announcement searching gives when finding a previously 
unknown trap will show you the portal even if there's an object 
on it.


  Summary:  

  Confused scroll of gold detection is easily the best on the 
plane of Fire.

  Cursed scrolls of gold detection don't require that you
disable/undisable your character and are very usable on 
the Planes of Earth and Air.  Multiple c?oGD are uniquely
suitable on the Plane of Water.


  So, except on the Plane of Fire, cursed scrolls of gold
detection save time.  Saving time is important on the Astral
Planes as you don't want to get out of trouble nearly as much as 
you want to *stay* out of trouble.


